This project gratefully reuses the Taiyin Ephemeris C++ core and the same
Wasm bridge used by its Dart Web binding. The astronomy, calendar, BaZi and
Ziwei results are calculated by that core, not a second JavaScript port.

We thank the authors and maintainers of the underlying astronomical theories,
scientific data, algorithms and open-source implementations. The core's
acknowledgments and provenance are reproduced in CORE-NOTICE. Copyright,
permission and disclaimer texts for core third-party software are retained
in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt. Please retain these materials when redistributing
a build. Generated binaries also incorporate the selected Emscripten SDK's
runtime; retain its applicable notices in binary release packaging.

The default development Wasm embeds the project's default Ziwei rule tables
and built-in runtime resources. External precise ephemeris files and fixed-star
catalogs are loaded separately by the application; distribute their respective
source/provenance notices when bundling them.

Core source: https://github.com/RedSC1/taiyin-ephemeris
